look at questions 1 to 5.

4
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:25,840
Good morning. Calder Lettings.
Daniel speaking. How can I help?

5
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:29,191
Oh, hi. I filled in the
form on your website

6
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:32,072
last week about renting
a one-bedroom flat,

7
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:35,480
but nobody's got back to
me, so I thought I'd just ring.

8
00:00:35,825 --> 00:00:40,740
Ah, sorry about that. We've had a bit of
a backlog. Let me take your details again,

9
00:00:40,989 --> 00:00:44,060
and I'll set you up properly on our system.
Can I have your name?

10
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:45,940
It's Megan Renneson.

11
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:52,360
Megan, and that's R-E-N-I-S-O-N?

12
00:00:52,759 --> 00:00:59,360
Nearly. Renneson has a
double N, so R-E-N-N-I-S-O-N.

13
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:03,081
Double N. Got it. Thanks.
And what do you do, Megan?

14
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:05,752
The landlords always
ask about employment.

15
00:01:06,404 --> 00:01:11,060
Sure. Well, until the spring, I was
a receptionist at a dental surgery,

16
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:14,042
and people still assume
I'm a dental nurse, but

17
00:01:14,066 --> 00:01:16,532
I've actually just
qualified as a paramedic.

18
00:01:17,129 --> 00:01:19,200
I started with the
ambulance service in May.

19
00:01:19,614 --> 00:01:23,040
Oh, well done.
And when are you hoping to move in?

20
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,249
So, my current tenancy
ends on the 31st of

21
00:01:26,273 --> 00:01:29,232
July, but I don't want
to rush into anything,

22
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,762
so I'll stay with
my sister for a bit.

23
00:01:31,786 --> 00:01:34,792
Um, she's away herself
until the middle of August,

24
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:38,780
so I'd say from the 23rd of August.
Not before that.

25
00:01:39,229 --> 00:01:44,300
The 23rd. That's good timing, actually.
A lot of our flats come free around then.

26
00:01:44,859 --> 00:01:46,680
Now, what's your budget per month?

27
00:01:47,204 --> 00:01:50,180
Well, on the online form, I put £900.

28
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:52,300
Mm-hmm.

29
00:01:52,334 --> 00:01:56,660
But I've been looking around, and I don't
think I'll find anything decent for that.

30
00:01:57,239 --> 00:02:02,780
So, I could stretch to £950. I really
can't go any higher than that, though.

31
00:02:03,149 --> 00:02:05,980
That's realistic for this area.
Is that including bills?

32
00:02:06,529 --> 00:02:09,419
No, that's just the rent.
I'll pay the bills on top.

33
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:14,560
Fine. Just so you know, there's a holding
deposit of one week's rent when you apply,

34
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,300
and then a full deposit of five
weeks' rent before you move in.

35
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,200
We'll also need a reference
from your current landlord.

36
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:25,360
That's no problem. I've always paid
on time, so she's happy to write one.

37
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:28,427
Great. And is there
anything the landlord would

38
00:02:28,451 --> 00:02:30,912
need to agree to? Any
special requirements?

39
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:35,392
Yes. Uh, I've got a pet. Not a
dog. Everyone assumes that.

40
00:02:35,416 --> 00:02:39,812
And it isn't a cat, either. I know
landlords worry about their carpets.

41
00:02:40,275 --> 00:02:43,280
It's a rabbit.
She lives indoors, in a big cage.

42
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,828
Ha ha! A rabbit! That
shouldn't put most of them

43
00:02:46,852 --> 00:02:50,212
off, but I'll make a note
so there are no surprises.

44
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,736
Right. I've got three flats
on my list at the moment

45
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:56,312
that might suit you. Shall
I tell you about them?

46
00:02:56,609 --> 00:03:00,880
Yes, please. Hang on, let me find a pen.
Okay, go ahead.

47
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:04,304
Before you hear the rest
of the conversation, you

48
00:03:04,328 --> 00:03:06,732
have some time to look
at questions six to ten.

49
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:47,435
Okay. The first one's on
Mill Lane, near the park.

50
00:03:47,459 --> 00:03:51,572
The rent is $875 a month, so
that's well within your budget.

51
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:57,140
Oh, nice. What floor is it on? I'd rather
not be on the ground floor, to be honest.

52
00:04:01,390 --> 00:04:04,935
Well, the advert says second floor, but
actually, that's wrong. I went round there on

53
00:04:04,959 --> 00:04:08,852
Monday, and it's on the third floor. It's the
top of the building, so it gets a lot of light.

54
00:04:09,190 --> 00:04:11,940
That sounds lovely. Is there a catch?

55
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:19,101
The main thing is that there's no lift, so
you'd be climbing three flights of stairs every

56
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:23,212
day. Parking's fine, there's a residence permit
scheme, and the boiler was replaced last year.

57
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:28,173
Three flights with the
shopping and the rabbit's cage.

58
00:04:28,197 --> 00:04:31,012
Hmm. Okay, what's
the second one?

59
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:34,813
That's on Carlton
Road, just by the station.

60
00:04:34,837 --> 00:04:39,380
$930 a month. It's been completely
refurbished, so… Completely?

61
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:48,277
Well, not quite. The bathroom wasn't touched.
That's about ten years old, and the carpets are the

62
00:04:48,301 --> 00:04:52,312
same. But there's a brand new kitchen. It was fitted
just last month, and it's beautifully designed.

63
00:04:52,710 --> 00:04:58,220
That's a big plus. I cook a lot. But is
it noisy, being so close to the station?

64
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:12,955
That's what everyone asks. Actually, the trains aren't the issue. The windows
are all double glazed. The problem is that the flat is directly above a

65
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:17,936
bakery, and they start work at about four in the morning. You'd wake up to
the smell of fresh bread, but you'd also hear the ovens and the delivery vans.

66
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:22,240
With my shifts, I'm sometimes
up at four anyway. And the third?

67
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:28,499
The third is in Orchard Court,
the new development by the river.

68
00:05:28,523 --> 00:05:33,640
That's $990, so a bit over… Yes,
that's more than I said I could pay.

69
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:40,220
I know, but it might be worth a look, because
the landlord said he may come down a little.

70
00:05:40,244 --> 00:05:44,132
It hasn't got a garden. There used to be a shared
one, but it's been turned into car parking.

71
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:47,538
But there's a really large
balcony, big enough for a

72
00:05:47,562 --> 00:05:50,332
table and chairs, and it
gets the sun all afternoon.

73
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:54,760
Oh, I'd love some outdoor space.
Is there any storage?

74
00:05:55,175 --> 00:05:58,580
Plenty. Each flat has its own
storeroom in the basement.

75
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:04,560
Okay. Could I see all three? Maybe
Carlton Road first, because of the kitchen?

76
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:08,038
Of course. I could do
Thursday afternoon, say, two

77
00:06:08,062 --> 00:06:11,172
o'clock, and then go
straight on to the other two.

78
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:15,920
Ah, I'm on a late shift on Thursday.
Friday morning would be better.

79
00:06:16,285 --> 00:06:18,575
Friday at ten, then. I'll
meet you outside the

80
00:06:18,599 --> 00:06:21,252
bakery, and I'll text you
the details this afternoon.

81
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:24,080
Perfect. Thanks so much, Daniel.

82
